WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:07.100
Just as the sun will come out tomorrow, so
too can we count on those magnificent beefcake

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:13.349
boys and gearhead girls in the Fast and the
Furious franchise to arrive with another action-packed

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:14.349
installment.

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:19.350
From a focus on family to celebrity cameos,
here are the things that happen in every single

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.254
Fast and Furious movie.

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:28.920
While Fast Five and Fast &amp; Furious 6 cemented
"family" as a highly memeable character motivation

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.210
for Vin Diesel's Dominic Toretto, "family"
has always been the third most important f-word

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.930
of the franchise, right behind "fast" and
"furious."

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.810
After all, the first film is about a loner
cop finding a community in Dom's DVD-player

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.970
stealing crew.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:48.380
And the sequel is about Paul Walker's Brian
trying to mend fences with his childhood best

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:53.059
friend, Roman, in a story that wouldn't play
out any differently if they were actually

00:00:53.059 --> 00:00:54.430
related by blood.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:58.890
Tokyo Drift is about carving out a place for
yourself apart from a familial legacy you

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.969
might not have wanted, and the fourth film
is about what happens when a member of your

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:06.750
family is murdered — you go on a street-racing
rampage.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.530
In short, long before Dom looked right at
the camera and told audiences around the world

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.530
—

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.240
"I don't have friends, I got family."

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.030
— Fast and the Furious has always been about
the family connections we make for ourselves.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:27.780
The Fast and the Furious franchise as it stands
today feels more like a James Bond spin-off

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.570
series than the adventures of a bunch of street-racing
dirtbags that we started with.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:37.880
Still, even as the stakes have gotten higher
and Dom's family has gotten bigger, a major

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.720
constant in the franchise is that most problems
can be solved with fast cars.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.310
It might seem silly to point this out — after
all, one of the two major adjectives in the

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:52.020
franchise's title is related to speed — but
considering how massive the set pieces have

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.220
become, it's comforting that the main solution
to any problem has always been fast cars driving

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.000
where you wouldn't expect cars to drive.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.780
Whether it's destroying the entire police
force of Rio de Janeiro in Fast Five or taking

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:08.470
out a nuclear submarine in Russia with the
use of an American muscle car, there's no

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:12.920
problem in the Fast and the Furious world
that can't be solved by living your life one

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.540
quarter-mile at a time.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:21.610
"Start out stealing DVD players and ends up
heisting 100 million dollars from Rio."

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.800
"Not bad, huh?"

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.030
Considering the utility of a properly engineered
vehicle in the Fast and the Furious franchise,

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:33.790
it's no surprise that the crew takes some
time to appreciate their fleet of their vehicles

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.360
whenever they can.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.760
The Fast Family are a bunch of gearheads at
heart, and that means their cars aren't just

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:45.360
tools for super-spy adventures — the cars
are a reflection of themselves.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.420
Before the franchise became as action-driven
as it is today, the cars were arguably the

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:55.200
biggest draw of the early films, and that
aesthetic appreciation remains a core driver

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.400
in the franchise.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.010
No matter how high the stakes are, there's
always time for the characters to pause and

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.790
admire the cars they'll be driving in upcoming
scenes.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:10.670
That moment arguably reaches its peak in Fate
of the Furious when Little Nobody takes the

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:15.690
Fast Family into a secret government warehouse
full of confiscated vehicles they can use

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.990
to rescue Dom.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:21.040
Just because the world is at stake doesn't
mean we can't take some time to peek under

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.040
the hood

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.459
Here's something you might not have noticed:
No good guy in the Fast and the Furious franchise

00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:29.830
has ever lost a fight.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:34.160
If that feels surprising, think about some
of the greatest smackdowns in the films.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:39.120
There's Dom fighting Hobbs in a garage during
Fast Five, Hobbs fighting Shaw early in Furious

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:44.820
7, or Dom fighting literally every other member
of his family in Fate of the Furious.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.400
But these impressive battles don't just belong
to the beefcakes.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.920
Brian somehow manages to beat Kiet in Furious
7, despite the fact the bad guy is played

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.319
by real-life Thai martial artist Tony Jaa.

00:03:57.319 --> 00:04:01.069
Most fights in the Fast and the Furious universe
either end with the good guy walking away

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:06.070
the clear victor, or the fight itself being
interrupted by circumstances outside of the

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.450
hero's control.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:11.650
With regards to that Hobbs and Shaw smackdown,
the fight only ends when Hobbs is knocked

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.270
out of a window by an explosion while covering
for Elena.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:18.790
When it comes to the Hobbs and Dom slugfest,
it gets interrupted before an unquestionable

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.090
victor can be crowned.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:25.750
As a result, there are rumors of a "can't
lose" contract for some of the actors.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:29.530
But whether or not that's true, the fact remains
that if you're a good guy in the world of

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:33.250
Fast and the Furious, no weapon raised against
you will prosper.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.030
Even comic relief Roman gets a moment in Fate
of the Furious where he knocks a guy off a

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:41.020
snowmobile with a car door before shooting
three other faceless goons.

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:46.950
The Fast and the Furious franchise has earned
a bit of a reputation for being needlessly

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.510
complex, which isn't really fair.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.700
After all, the order of the films are simple.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:55.650
If you want to watch it chronologically, you
just watch The Fast and the Furious, the short

00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:02.850
film Turbo Charged Prelude to 2 Fast 2 Furious,
2 Fast 2 Furious, the short film Los Bandoleros,

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:08.470
Fast &amp; Furious, Fast Five, Fast &amp; Furious
6 until the post-credits scene, then watch

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.740
half of Fast &amp; Furious: Tokyo Drift.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.771
After that, take a break, for sure, then watch
the post-credits to Fast &amp; Furious 6, watch

00:05:16.771 --> 00:05:22.180
most of the rest of Fast &amp; Furious: Tokyo
Drift, watch Furious 7 until Dom wants to

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:27.190
go to Tokyo, then finish watching the very
end of Fast &amp; Furious: Tokyo Drift before

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:30.210
completing Furious 7 and enjoying Fate of
the Furious.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:35.290
Oh, and watch Better Luck Tomorrow if you're
a completionist and want to see the origin

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.290
of Han.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.450
Simple, right?

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:41.901
Okay, maybe the franchise has gotten pretty
complex, but that's what happens when you

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:46.240
keep building on the continuity without writing
characters off between films.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:51.590
Each installment showcases either the appearance
of an old character or at least a tossed-off

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.110
mention to previous films.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:57.740
It can take the form of Brian investigating
Fast &amp; Furious villain Braga midway through

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:02.900
Fast &amp; Furious 6, or Dom relying on his Fast
Five crew in Fate of the Furious.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.979
But no matter who shows up or when, you can
always count on some familiar faces to pop

00:06:07.979 --> 00:06:10.120
up in a Fast and the Furious film.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:16.510
With each new Fast and the Furious film's
budget ballooning into the hundreds of millions,

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:20.840
it's no stretch to say the movies are known
for their jaw-dropping action.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:24.760
But even when the budget was in the sub-hundred
million range, the filmmakers still found

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.570
a way to pack plenty of action into the films.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:31.820
The Fast and the Furious features a climax
in which one of Dom's men is wired tight to

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:35.280
a semi-truck while the driver shoots a shotgun
at Dom's crew.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:40.130
Meanwhile, 2 Fast 2 Furious ends with Roman
and Brian launching a car onto a boat like

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.900
someone trying to weaponize the Dukes of Hazzard
boys.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:48.070
And Tokyo Drift finds Han and the ostensible
protagonist, Sean Boswell, drifting through

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:52.160
the Tokyo streets as crowds of people part
like the Red Sea.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:57.210
By the time Fast Five rolls around, the films
have gotten so big that Brian and Dom are

00:06:57.210 --> 00:07:01.550
destroying Rio with a vault that they're using
like a wrecking ball.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:06.479
There's no telling what insane set pieces
we can expect in the future, but if there's

00:07:06.479 --> 00:07:11.290
anything that lives up to Dom leaping across
a bridge from his car to save Letty from getting

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.889
knocked off a tank, we can all die happy.

00:07:14.979 --> 00:07:21.200
At its core, the first Fast and the Furious
film is a movie with simple pleasures in mind.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.810
There are cars, and they will go fast.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.419
There are tough guys, and they will win fights.

00:07:26.419 --> 00:07:31.870
There are beautiful girls in bikinis that
are big fans of both cars and tough guys,

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.940
and they will dance.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:38.050
Even as the films have rounded out the cast,
those core ideals remain the same.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:42.850
No matter what destinations the Fast Family
visit, there's always going to be time for

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:47.710
a race, and there are always going to be beautiful
women that are excited to watch.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:52.220
Even while Dom was working to restore Letty's
memory in Fast &amp; Furious 6, there was a London

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:55.640
street race that featured plenty of car girls.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:00.550
It might be one of the strongest connective
tissues uniting the various locales in the

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:05.960
franchise, a signifier of car culture that
surpasses any sort of division or geographical

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:06.960
line.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:10.949
Or, most likely, it's because the Fast and
the Furious directors like shooting scenes

00:08:10.949 --> 00:08:12.730
with gorgeous women in exotic locales.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:18.100
It's not all seriousness and widescreen action
when you're a part of Dom's crew.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.930
Sure, there's a chance that you'll be blown
up by a former SAS operative or that you'll

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:26.920
fall onto an endless airplane runway in the
middle of a gun battle, but there are good

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:27.920
times, too.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.669
After all, Dom knows how to throw a killer
party, even if the beer selection is limited.

00:08:31.669 --> 00:08:34.070
"You can have any brew you want.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.200
As long as it's a corona."

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.259
Every film in the Fast and the Furious franchise
has made time for a party, whether it's the

00:08:41.259 --> 00:08:45.649
now traditional post-action barbecue or the
low-budget house party of The Fast and the

00:08:45.649 --> 00:08:46.749
Furious.

00:08:46.749 --> 00:08:51.980
Even Furious 7, grim as everything was in
the wake of Han's untimely murder, still found

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:55.300
time to have a party DJ-ed by T-Pain in Abu
Dhabi.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:09:00.079
When you live your life one quarter-mile at
a time, you've got to leave room to celebrate.

